IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc9-support`
IMPORT `ccc9-sexual-evidence`

-- ccc9-records.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), ss 278.1 to 278.31: records and therapeutic records of a complainant or witness: production to the accused of records held
-- by a third party (ss 278.11 to 278.19) and by the prosecutor (ss 278.2 to 278.28), and their admissibility when held by the accused (ss 278.29 to 278.31).
-- Sections 278.32 onwards (ccc10) are the other part's: the seam of PLAN.md R5, `s 278.3 an application for a hearing on records in the accused's possession has been made`, is answered here.
-- LAYER 1: the law as the text states it, from no one's point of view. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: see ccc9-assault-officer.l4 (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled) and ccc9-sexual-evidence.l4. The "may" functions (a judge's power with an "if" gate) answer NOTHING when the gate
-- fails (ruling of 2026-11-12); a duty whose "if" gate fails, a flat negative and a bare "must" not met answer JUST FALSE; a bar or duty limited to a described scope answers NOTHING outside it.
-- Provisions that address only the judge, the prosecutor or the clerk are encoded for what they decide and for what they mean to the accused; the accused's own duties
-- (the application, the 60 days, the service, the copy to the complainant, the restriction on use, the publication bans) are rules with their time limits.
-- SEAMS taken as inputs: `by s 787(1)` (the penalty for a summary-conviction offence: ccc29); the judge's satisfaction and the facts of an application are plain facts the person states.
-- `s 2 complainant` and the like are not needed as inputs: the text's "complainant" is the person the record relates to, stated as a fact.

-- The acts of the regulative rules of this module (every constructor begins with its section label).
DECLARE `s 278.12 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.12(1) make an application for production to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried`
    `s 278.12(5) serve the application and a subpoena on the persons the subsection names`
    `s 278.12(6) order that the application be served on any person to whom the judge considers the record or therapeutic record may relate`
    `s 278.13(1) hold a hearing in camera to determine whether to order production to the court for review by the judge`
    `s 278.13(3) inform the person of their right to be represented by counsel as soon as feasible`
    `s 278.14(2) consider the salutary and deleterious effects of the determination on the accused's right to make a full answer and defence and on the right to privacy, personal security and equality of the complainant or witness and of any other person to whom the record relates`
    `s 278.15(1) review the record or the part of it in the absence of the parties to determine whether it should be produced to the accused`
    `s 278.15(2) hold a hearing in camera`
    `s 278.16(4) impose conditions on the production to protect the interests of justice`
    `s 278.16(5) direct that a copy of the record or therapeutic record, or the part, be provided to the prosecutor`
    `s 278.16(6) use the record in any other proceedings`
    `s 278.17(1) provide reasons for ordering or refusing to order the production`
    `s 278.18(1) publish, broadcast or transmit in any way a matter listed in subsection (1)`
    `s 278.2(2) produce the thing to the accused`
    `s 278.2(3) notify the accused that the record is in the prosecutor's possession or control, without disclosing its contents`
    `s 278.2(3) disclose the contents of the record in notifying the accused`
    `s 278.21(1) make an application for production to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried`
    `s 278.21(5) serve the application on the persons the subsection names`
    `s 278.21(6) order that the application be served on any person to whom the judge considers the record or therapeutic record may relate`
    `s 278.22(1) hold a hearing in camera to determine whether to order production to the court for review by the judge`
    `s 278.22(3) inform the person of their right to be represented by counsel as soon as feasible`
    `s 278.23(2) consider the salutary and deleterious effects of the determination on the accused's right to make a full answer and defence and on the right to privacy, personal security and equality of the complainant or witness and of any other person to whom the record relates`
    `s 278.24(1) review the record or the part of it in the absence of the parties to determine whether it should be produced to the accused`
    `s 278.24(2) hold a hearing in camera`
    `s 278.25(4) impose conditions on the production to protect the interests of justice`
    `s 278.25(5) use the record in any other proceedings`
    `s 278.26(1) provide reasons for ordering or refusing to order the production`
    `s 278.27(1) publish, broadcast or transmit in any way a matter listed in subsection (1)`
    `s 278.3(4) consider the application with the jury and the public excluded`
    `s 278.3(6) cause a copy of the application to be given to the complainant by a person other than the accused`
    `s 278.31(1) exclude the jury and the public from the hearing`
    `s 278.31(3) inform the complainant of their right to be represented by counsel as soon as feasible`
    `s 278.31(4) determine whether the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) and provide reasons`


§ `Part VIII -- Definitions for ss 278.11 to 278.36 (s 278.1)`

-- "record means any form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy and includes medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption and social services records,
-- personal journals and diaries, and any record containing personal information the production or disclosure of which is protected by any other Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature, but does not include records made
-- by persons responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence." Read as the keel reads "means ... and includes ..." (its fork F2): the means part and the listed extension together are closed.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.1; s 278.1 record
-- src:5305 | record means any form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy and includes medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption and social services records, personal journals and diaries, and any record containing personal information the production or disclosure of which is protected by any other Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature, but does not include records made by persons responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence. (dossier)
@ref Criminal Code s 278.1 "record" (src:5305-5305)
GIVEN `it is a form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption or social services record, a personal journal or diary, or a record containing personal information protected by another Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a record made by a person responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.1 the thing is a record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a record made by a person responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include records made by persons responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence"
        IF `it is a form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy` OR `it is a medical, education, employment, child welfare, adoption or social services record, a personal journal or diary, or a record containing personal information protected by another Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "record means any form of record that contains personal information for which there is a reasonable expectation of privacy"

-- "therapeutic record means any form of record, regardless of its contents, that was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling provided by a health care professional who is entitled under the laws
-- of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling."
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.1 therapeutic record
-- src:5306 | therapeutic record means any form of record, regardless of its contents, that was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling provided by a health care professional who is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling. (dossier thérapeutique)
@ref Criminal Code s 278.1 "therapeutic record" (src:5306-5306)
GIVEN `it was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the treatment, therapy or counselling was provided by a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the health care professional is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.1 the thing is a therapeutic record` MEANS
    IF `it was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling` AND `the treatment, therapy or counselling was provided by a health care professional` AND `the health care professional is entitled under the laws of a province or of a foreign state to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "therapeutic record means any form of record, regardless of its contents, that was produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling"

§ `Part VIII -- Production to the accused of records held by a third party (s 278.11)`

-- The offences are named by section number (R1; any subsection of a named section) "or any other offence ... that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose" (a fact the person states).
-- The same list stands in s 278.11(1)(a), s 278.2(1)(a) and s 278.29(1)(a): it is written once.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.11(1)(a)
-- src:5311 | (a) an offence under section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 173, 213, 271, 272, 273, 279.01, 279.011, 279.02, 279.03, 286.1, 286.2 or 286.3 or any other offence under this Act, or any other Act of Parliament, that is of a sexual nature or that is committed for a sexual purpose;
@ref Criminal Code s 278.11(1)(a) (src:5311-5311)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 278.11(1)(a) the offence is one of those named` MEANS
       offence's `section` EQUALS 151
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 152
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 153.1
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 155
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 160
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 170
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 171
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 172
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 173
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 213
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 271
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 272
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 273
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 279.01
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 279.011
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 279.02
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 279.03
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 286.1
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 286.2
     OR offence's `section` EQUALS 286.3

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.11(1)(b)
-- src:5312 | (b) any offence under this Act, as it read from time to time before the day on which this paragraph comes into force, if the conduct alleged would be an offence referred to in paragraph (a) if it occurred on or after that day.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.11(1)(b) (src:5312-5312)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence under this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which paragraph 278.11(1)(b) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct alleged would be an offence referred to in paragraph (a) if it occurred on or after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 278.11(1)(b) the earlier offence is one to which the section applies` MEANS
    `the offence is an offence under this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which paragraph 278.11(1)(b) comes into force` AND `the conduct alleged would be an offence referred to in paragraph (a) if it occurred on or after that day`

-- The proceedings: in respect of one or more offences, at least one of which is within (a) or (b).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.11(1)
-- src:5309 | Records and therapeutic records possessed by third party
-- src:5310 | 278.11 (1) Except in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19, no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant or a witness that is in the possession or control of a third party shall be produced to an accused in any proceedings in respect of any of the following offences or in any proceedings in respect of two or more offences at least one of which is any of the following offences:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.11(1) (src:5309-5310)
DECLARE `s 278.11(1) offence in the proceedings` HAS
    `the offence`   IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is an earlier offence to which paragraph (b) applies`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.11(1)
-- src:5309 | Records and therapeutic records possessed by third party
-- src:5310 | 278.11 (1) Except in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19, no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant or a witness that is in the possession or control of a third party shall be produced to an accused in any proceedings in respect of any of the following offences or in any proceedings in respect of two or more offences at least one of which is any of the following offences:
