GIVEN offences IS A LIST OF `s 278.11(1) offence in the proceedings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 278.11(1) the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the section applies` MEANS
    any (GIVEN o YIELD `s 278.11(1)(a) the offence is one of those named` (o's `the offence`) OR o's `the offence is, apart from those named, an offence of a sexual nature or one committed for a sexual purpose` OR o's `the offence is an earlier offence to which paragraph (b) applies`) offences

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.11(2)
-- src:5313 | Definition of third party
-- src:5314 | (2) In subsection (1), third party means a person other than the prosecutor or the accused.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.11(2) (src:5313-5314)
GIVEN `the person is the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.11(2) the person is a third party` MEANS
    IF `the person is the prosecutor` OR `the person is the accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "third party means a person other than the prosecutor or the accused"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (1): JUST TRUE: production to the accused is barred, except in accordance with ss 278.12 to 278.19. JUST FALSE: it is produced in accordance with them (the text's "Except in accordance with"). NOTHING: the record, the holder or the proceedings are outside the section.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.11(1)
-- src:5309 | Records and therapeutic records possessed by third party
-- src:5310 | 278.11 (1) Except in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19, no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant or a witness that is in the possession or control of a third party shall be produced to an accused in any proceedings in respect of any of the following offences or in any proceedings in respect of two or more offences at least one of which is any of the following offences:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.11(1) (src:5309-5310)
GIVEN `the thing is a record or a therapeutic record, by s 278.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it relates to a complainant or a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the possession or control of a third party, by s 278.11(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the section applies, by s 278.11(1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the production is in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.11(1) production to the accused is barred except in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is a record or a therapeutic record, by s 278.1` EQUALS NOTHING OR `it is in the possession or control of a third party, by s 278.11(2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is a record, or the holder a third party, is itself not covered
        IF (`the thing is a record or a therapeutic record, by s 278.1` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `it relates to a complainant or a witness`) OR (`it is in the possession or control of a third party, by s 278.11(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the section applies, by s 278.11(1)(a) and (b)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant or a witness that is in the possession or control of a third party shall be produced to an accused in any proceedings in respect of any of the following offences"
        IF `the production is in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in accordance with sections 278.12 to 278.19"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Part VIII -- The application for production (s 278.12)`

-- The text states no time limit for making the application, so the rule carries no WITHIN.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.12(1)
-- src:5315 | Application for production
-- src:5316 | 278.12 (1) An accused who seeks production of a record or therapeutic record referred to in section 278.11 must make an application for its production to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(1) (src:5315-5316)
GIVEN `the accused seeks production of a record or therapeutic record referred to in section 278.11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.12(1) the accused who seeks production must apply to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried` MEANS
    IF `the accused seeks production of a record or therapeutic record referred to in section 278.11`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who seeks production of a record or therapeutic record referred to in section 278.11 must make an application for its production to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.12(1)
-- src:5315 | Application for production
-- src:5316 | 278.12 (1) An accused who seeks production of a record or therapeutic record referred to in section 278.11 must make an application for its production to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(1) (src:5315-5316)
GIVEN `the accused seeks production of a record or therapeutic record referred to in section 278.11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.12(1) the accused's duty to apply to the trial judge` MEANS
    IF `s 278.12(1) the accused who seeks production must apply to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried` `the accused seeks production of a record or therapeutic record referred to in section 278.11` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused`
         MUST `s 278.12(1) make an application for production to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 278.12(1): no application for production was made to the judge before whom the accused is to be, or is being, tried"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no duty arises on these facts: this is not a finding about any other case (the decision function answers NOTHING there)

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.12(2)
-- src:5317 | No application in other proceedings
-- src:5318 | (2) For greater certainty, the application referred to in subsection (1) must not be made to a judge, provincial court judge or justice presiding at any other proceedings, including a preliminary inquiry.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(2) (src:5317-5318)
GIVEN `it is the application referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.12(2) the application may be made to a judge, provincial court judge or justice presiding at any other proceedings` MEANS
    IF `it is the application referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the application referred to in subsection (1) must not be made to a judge, provincial court judge or justice presiding at any other proceedings, including a preliminary inquiry"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the application referred to in subsection (1) must not be made to a judge, provincial court judge or justice presiding at any other proceedings, including a preliminary inquiry"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.12(3); s 278.12(3)(a); s 278.12(3)(b); s 278.12(3)(c)
-- src:5319 | Form and content
-- src:5320 | (3) The application must be made in writing and must set out
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(3) (src:5319-5320)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application sets out particulars identifying the record or the therapeutic record that the accused seeks to have produced and the name of the person who has possession or control of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing sought is a therapeutic record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the case of a record, the application sets out the grounds on which the accused relies to establish that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the case of a therapeutic record, the application sets out the grounds on which the accused relies to establish that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` MEANS
    IF     `the application is made in writing`
       AND `the application sets out particulars identifying the record or the therapeutic record that the accused seeks to have produced and the name of the person who has possession or control of it`
       AND (IF `the thing sought is a therapeutic record`
            THEN `in the case of a therapeutic record, the application sets out the grounds on which the accused relies to establish that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt`
            ELSE `in the case of a record, the application sets out the grounds on which the accused relies to establish that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be made in writing and must set out"

-- src:5324 | Insufficient grounds
-- src:5325 | (4) Any one or more of the following assertions by the accused are not sufficient on their own to establish that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify or that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused’s guilt:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(4) (src:5324-5325)
DECLARE `s 278.12(4) assertion` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.12(4)(a) that the record or therapeutic record exists`
    `s 278.12(4)(b) that the record or therapeutic record relates to medical or psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling that the complainant or witness has received or is receiving`
    `s 278.12(4)(c) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the incident that is the subject matter of the proceedings`
    `s 278.12(4)(d) that the record or therapeutic record may disclose a prior inconsistent statement of the complainant or witness`
    `s 278.12(4)(e) that the record or therapeutic record may relate to the credibility of the complainant or witness`
    `s 278.12(4)(f) that the record or therapeutic record may relate to the reliability of the testimony of the complainant or witness merely because the complainant or witness has received or is receiving psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling`
    `s 278.12(4)(g) that the record or therapeutic record may reveal allegations of sexual abuse of the complainant by a person other than the accused`
    `s 278.12(4)(h) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the sexual activity of the complainant with any person, including the accused`
    `s 278.12(4)(i) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the presence or absence of a recent complaint`
    `s 278.12(4)(j) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the complainant's sexual reputation`
    `s 278.12(4)(k) that the record or therapeutic record was made close in time to a complaint or to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused`
    `s 278.12(4) any other assertion`

-- Not sufficient "on their own": JUST TRUE when every assertion made is one of the listed ones. NOTHING when no assertion is made, or when another assertion is also made: the text says nothing about what suffices.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.12(4); s 278.12(4)(a); s 278.12(4)(b); s 278.12(4)(c); s 278.12(4)(d); s 278.12(4)(e); s 278.12(4)(f); s 278.12(4)(g); s 278.12(4)(h); s 278.12(4)(i); s 278.12(4)(j); s 278.12(4)(k)
-- src:5324 | Insufficient grounds
-- src:5325 | (4) Any one or more of the following assertions by the accused are not sufficient on their own to establish that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify or that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused’s guilt:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(4) (src:5324-5325)
GIVEN assertions IS A LIST OF `s 278.12(4) assertion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF null assertions THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no assertion is made, and the text says what only the listed assertions amount to
        IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS `s 278.12(4) any other assertion`) assertions THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names eleven assertions and says nothing of any other
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (5): "The accused shall serve the application on ... at least 60 days before the hearing ... or within any shorter interval that the judge may allow in the interests of justice." A bare "shall" not met is the text's no for this question (fork F).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.12(5)
-- src:5337 | Service of application and subpoena
-- src:5338 | (5) The accused shall serve the application on the prosecutor, on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record, on the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and on any other person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates, at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in subsection 278.13(1) or within any shorter interval that the judge may allow in the interests of justice. The accused shall also serve a subpoena issued under Part XXII in Form 16.1 on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record at the same time as the application is served.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(5) (src:5337-5338)
GIVEN `the application has been served on the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been served on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been served on the complainant or witness, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is another person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been served on that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a subpoena issued under Part XXII in Form 16.1 was served on the person who has possession or control at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was served` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.12(5) the accused has served the application as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the application has been served on the prosecutor`
       AND `the application has been served on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record`
       AND `the application has been served on the complainant or witness, as the case may be`
       AND ((NOT `there is another person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates`) OR `the application has been served on that other person`)
       AND `a subpoena issued under Part XXII in Form 16.1 was served on the person who has possession or control at the same time`
       AND `s 276.01(4) the copy was given and filed at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows` `the day the application was served` `the day of the hearing` `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accused shall serve the application on the prosecutor, on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record"

-- The accused's duty as a rule, with its period: WITHIN the days from the day the application is made until 60 days before the hearing. Where the judge allows a shorter interval the text gives its length to the judge: no period is stated here.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.12(5)
-- src:5337 | Service of application and subpoena
-- src:5338 | (5) The accused shall serve the application on the prosecutor, on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record, on the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and on any other person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates, at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in subsection 278.13(1) or within any shorter interval that the judge may allow in the interests of justice. The accused shall also serve a subpoena issued under Part XXII in Form 16.1 on the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record at the same time as the application is served.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.12(5) (src:5337-5338)
GIVEN `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.12(5) the accused's duty to serve the application` MEANS
    IF `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`
    THEN FULFILLED   -- the interval is the judge's to allow and the text states no length: no period is stated here (not a finding that the duty is met)
    ELSE PARTY `the accused`
         MUST `s 278.12(5) serve the application and a subpoena on the persons the subsection names`
         WITHIN (`s 270 helper: the days from the earlier date to the later date` `the day the application is made` `the day of the hearing` MINUS 60)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 278.12(5): the application was not served at least 60 days before the hearing"

