§ `Part VIII -- Order for production to the judge for review (s 278.14)`

-- (1): the judge MAY order production to the court for review "if, after the hearing ..., the judge is satisfied that" (a), (b), (c). A "may" function with an "if" gate: NOTHING when the gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12; fork in NOTES.md).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.14(1); s 278.14(1)(a); s 278.14(1)(b); s 278.14(1)(c)
-- src:5351 | Order — production to judge
-- src:5352 | 278.14 (1) The judge may order the person who has possession or control of the record or therapeutic record to produce it, or any part of it, to the court for review by the judge if, after the hearing referred to in section 278.13, the judge is satisfied that
@ref Criminal Code s 278.14(1) (src:5351-5352)
GIVEN `the application was made in accordance with subsections 278.12(2) to (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has established that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify, or that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the production of all or any part of the record or therapeutic record is necessary in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.14(1) the judge may order production of the record or therapeutic record to the court for review` MEANS
    IF `the application was made in accordance with subsections 278.12(2) to (6)` AND `the accused has established that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify, or that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt` AND `the production of all or any part of the record or therapeutic record is necessary in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, after the hearing referred to in section 278.13, the judge is satisfied that"

-- src:5356 | Factors to be considered
-- src:5357 | (2) In determining whether to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, for review, the judge shall consider the salutary and deleterious effects of the determination on the accused’s right to make a full answer and defence and on the right to privacy, personal security and equality of the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and of any other person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates. In particular, the judge shall take the following factors into account:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.14(2) (src:5356-5357)
DECLARE `s 278.14(2) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.14(2)(a) the extent to which the record or therapeutic record is necessary for the accused to make a full answer and defence`
    `s 278.14(2)(b) the probative value of the record or therapeutic record`
    `s 278.14(2)(c) the nature and extent of the reasonable expectation of privacy with respect to the record or therapeutic record`
    `s 278.14(2)(d) whether production of the record or therapeutic record is based on a discriminatory belief or bias`
    `s 278.14(2)(e) the potential prejudice to the personal dignity and right to privacy of any person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates`
    `s 278.14(2)(f) society's interest in encouraging the reporting of sexual offences`
    `s 278.14(2)(g) society's interest in encouraging the obtaining of treatment by complainants of sexual offences`
    `s 278.14(2)(h) the effect of the determination on the integrity of the trial process`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.14(2)(a); s 278.14(2)(b); s 278.14(2)(c); s 278.14(2)(d); s 278.14(2)(e); s 278.14(2)(f); s 278.14(2)(g); s 278.14(2)(h)
