    `s 278.14(2) the judge shall take the factor into account` factor

-- src:5378 | Conditions
-- src:5379 | (4) If the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused, the judge may impose conditions on the production to protect the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests of the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and of any other person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates, including, for example, the following conditions:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.16(4) (src:5378-5379)
DECLARE `s 278.16(4) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.16(4)(a) that the record or therapeutic record be edited as directed by the judge`
    `s 278.16(4)(b) that a copy of the record or therapeutic record, rather than the original, be produced`
    `s 278.16(4)(c) that the accused and counsel for the accused not disclose the contents of the record or therapeutic record to any other person, except with the approval of the court`
    `s 278.16(4)(d) that the record or therapeutic record be viewed only at the offices of the court`
    `s 278.16(4)(e) that no copies of the record or therapeutic record be made or that restrictions be imposed on the number of copies of it that may be made`
    `s 278.16(4)(f) that information regarding any person named in the record or therapeutic record, such as their address, telephone number and place of employment, be severed from the record or therapeutic record`
    `s 278.16(4) another condition`

-- (4): the judge MAY impose conditions on the production "to protect the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests" ... "including, for example," the six listed.
-- A listed condition is JUST TRUE; another is JUST TRUE only if it protects those interests; NOTHING otherwise and outside an order for production to the accused.
