-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.16(5)
-- src:5386 | Copy to prosecutor
-- src:5387 | (5) If the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused, the judge shall direct that a copy of the record or therapeutic record, or the part, be provided to the prosecutor, unless the judge determines that it is not in the interests of justice to do so.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.16(5) (src:5386-5387)
GIVEN presiding IS A Party
      `the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has not determined that it is not in the interests of justice to provide a copy to the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.16(5) the judge's duty to direct a copy to the prosecutor` MEANS
    IF `s 278.16(5) the judge shall direct that a copy be provided to the prosecutor` `the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused` `the judge has not determined that it is not in the interests of justice to provide a copy to the prosecutor` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY presiding
         MUST `s 278.16(5) direct that a copy of the record or therapeutic record, or the part, be provided to the prosecutor`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY presiding BECAUSE "s 278.16(5): no direction was given that a copy be provided to the prosecutor"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no duty arises on these facts: the decision function answers JUST FALSE there, the text's own "if" being unmet, which is not a finding about any other case

-- "The record or therapeutic record, or the part of it, that is produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1) must not be used in any other proceedings."
-- The text names only an order under subsection (1) (a record), not subsection (2) (a therapeutic record): encoded as written (finding in NOTES.md). JUST TRUE: use in other proceedings is barred.
