-- src:5413 | 278.2 (1) Except in accordance with sections 278.21 to 278.28, no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant or a witness that is in the possession or control of the prosecutor shall be produced to an accused in any proceedings in respect of any of the following offences or in any proceedings in respect of two or more offences at least one of which is any of the following offences:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.2(1) (src:5412-5413)
GIVEN `the thing is a record or a therapeutic record, by s 278.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it relates to a complainant or a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the possession or control of the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the section applies, by s 278.2(1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the production is in accordance with sections 278.21 to 278.28` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.2(1) production to the accused is barred except in accordance with sections 278.21 to 278.28` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing is a record or a therapeutic record, by s 278.1` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is a record or a therapeutic record is itself not covered
        IF (`the thing is a record or a therapeutic record, by s 278.1` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `it relates to a complainant or a witness`) OR (NOT `it is in the possession or control of the prosecutor`) OR (NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an offence to which the section applies, by s 278.2(1)(a) and (b)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant or a witness that is in the possession or control of the prosecutor shall be produced to an accused in any proceedings in respect of any of the following offences"
        IF `the production is in accordance with sections 278.21 to 278.28` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in accordance with sections 278.21 to 278.28"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 278.2(2) what the prosecutor may produce` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.2(2)(a) a record or part of a record`
    `s 278.2(2)(b) a record or therapeutic record, or a part of one`
    `s 278.2(2)(c) any communication between the accused and the complainant`

-- (2): the prosecutor MAY produce to the accused (a) a record or part of a record "if the prosecutor intends to adduce the record or part in court or if the record or part directly relates to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge";
-- (b) a record or therapeutic record, or a part, "if the complainant or witness to whom it relates agrees to its disclosure to the accused"; (c) any communication between the accused and the complainant.
-- A "may" function with an "if" gate: NOTHING when the gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12; fork in NOTES.md).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.2(2); s 278.2(2)(a); s 278.2(2)(b); s 278.2(2)(c)
-- src:5416 | Permitted production
-- src:5417 | (2) The prosecutor may produce to the accused
@ref Criminal Code s 278.2(2) (src:5416-5417)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 278.2(2) what the prosecutor may produce`
      `the prosecutor intends to adduce the record or part in court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record or part directly relates to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant or witness to whom it relates agrees to its disclosure to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.2(2) the prosecutor may produce the thing to the accused` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 278.2(2)(a) a record or part of a record` THEN
        IF `the prosecutor intends to adduce the record or part in court` OR `the record or part directly relates to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the prosecutor intends to adduce the record or part in court or if the record or part directly relates to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused"
    WHEN `s 278.2(2)(b) a record or therapeutic record, or a part of one` THEN
        IF `the complainant or witness to whom it relates agrees to its disclosure to the accused` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the complainant or witness to whom it relates agrees to its disclosure to the accused"
    WHEN `s 278.2(2)(c) any communication between the accused and the complainant` THEN JUST TRUE

-- The power as a rule: the prosecutor MAY produce it (no period: a permission not used lapses without consequence).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.2(2)
-- src:5416 | Permitted production
-- src:5417 | (2) The prosecutor may produce to the accused
@ref Criminal Code s 278.2(2) (src:5416-5417)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 278.2(2) what the prosecutor may produce`
      `the prosecutor intends to adduce the record or part in court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record or part directly relates to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant or witness to whom it relates agrees to its disclosure to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.2(2) the prosecutor's power to produce the thing to the accused` MEANS
    IF `s 278.2(2) the prosecutor may produce the thing to the accused` thing `the prosecutor intends to adduce the record or part in court` `the record or part directly relates to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused` `the complainant or witness to whom it relates agrees to its disclosure to the accused` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the prosecutor`
         MAY `s 278.2(2) produce the thing to the accused`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no power arises on these facts: this is not a finding that production is barred (the decision function answers NOTHING there)

-- "Subject to subsection (2)": where the prosecutor produces it under (2) the duty is limited by its own wording (NOTHING). The text states no time limit.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.2(3)
-- src:5421 | Duty of prosecutor to give notice
-- src:5422 | (3) Subject to subsection (2), if a record or therapeutic record in respect of which this section applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor, the prosecutor shall notify the accused that it is in the prosecutor’s possession or control but, in doing so, the prosecutor shall not disclose its contents.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.2(3) (src:5421-5422)
GIVEN `a record or therapeutic record in respect of which section 278.2 applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor does not produce it to the accused under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.2(3) the prosecutor shall notify the accused that the record is in the prosecutor's possession or control` MEANS
    IF `a record or therapeutic record in respect of which section 278.2 applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor` AND `the prosecutor does not produce it to the accused under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a record or therapeutic record in respect of which this section applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor, the prosecutor shall notify the accused that it is in the prosecutor's possession or control but, in doing so, the prosecutor shall not disclose its contents"

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.2(3)
-- src:5421 | Duty of prosecutor to give notice
-- src:5422 | (3) Subject to subsection (2), if a record or therapeutic record in respect of which this section applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor, the prosecutor shall notify the accused that it is in the prosecutor’s possession or control but, in doing so, the prosecutor shall not disclose its contents.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.2(3) (src:5421-5422)
GIVEN `a record or therapeutic record in respect of which section 278.2 applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor does not produce it to the accused under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.2(3) the prosecutor's duty to notify the accused` MEANS
    IF `s 278.2(3) the prosecutor shall notify the accused that the record is in the prosecutor's possession or control` `a record or therapeutic record in respect of which section 278.2 applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor` `the prosecutor does not produce it to the accused under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the prosecutor`
         MUST `s 278.2(3) notify the accused that the record is in the prosecutor's possession or control, without disclosing its contents`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the prosecutor` BECAUSE "s 278.2(3): the accused was not notified that the record is in the prosecutor's possession or control, or its contents were disclosed"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no duty arises on these facts: this is not a finding about any other case (the decision function answers NOTHING there)

-- The non-disclosure limb of (3): "but, in doing so, the prosecutor shall not disclose its contents". "In doing so" ties the bar to the notice the first limb requires, and the sentence opens "Subject to subsection (2)":
-- so it has the first limb's gate (the record is in the prosecutor's possession or control; the prosecutor does not produce it under (2)). JUST TRUE: the notice discloses the contents. The text says what is barred and not what is allowed, so a notice that does not disclose is not answered (NOTHING, as for s 278.16(6)).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.2(3)
-- src:5421 | Duty of prosecutor to give notice
-- src:5422 | (3) Subject to subsection (2), if a record or therapeutic record in respect of which this section applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor, the prosecutor shall notify the accused that it is in the prosecutor’s possession or control but, in doing so, the prosecutor shall not disclose its contents.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.2(3) (src:5421-5422)
GIVEN `a record or therapeutic record in respect of which section 278.2 applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor does not produce it to the accused under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor's notice to the accused discloses the contents of the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.2(3) the prosecutor shall not disclose the contents of the record in notifying the accused` MEANS
    IF `a record or therapeutic record in respect of which section 278.2 applies is in the possession or control of the prosecutor` AND `the prosecutor does not produce it to the accused under subsection (2)` AND `the prosecutor's notice to the accused discloses the contents of the record`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but, in doing so, the prosecutor shall not disclose its contents"

-- The bar as a rule: the prosecutor SHANT disclose the contents in the notice; no time limit, so no WITHIN.
