-- src:5435 | (4) Any one or more of the following assertions by the accused are not sufficient on their own to establish that the record is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify or that the therapeutic record contains evidence that could raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused’s guilt:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.21(4) (src:5434-5435)
GIVEN assertions IS A LIST OF `s 278.12(4) assertion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.21(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` MEANS
    `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` assertions

-- (5): "The accused shall serve the application on ... at least 60 days before the hearing ... or within any shorter interval that the judge may allow in the interests of justice." A bare "shall" not met is the text's no for this question (fork F).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.21(5)
-- src:5447 | Service of application
-- src:5448 | (5) The accused shall serve the application on the prosecutor, on the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and on any other person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates, at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in subsection 278.22(1) or within any shorter interval that the judge may allow in the interests of justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.21(5) (src:5447-5448)
GIVEN `the application has been served on the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been served on the complainant or witness, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is another person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been served on that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was served` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.21(5) the accused has served the application as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the application has been served on the prosecutor`
       AND `the application has been served on the complainant or witness, as the case may be`
       AND ((NOT `there is another person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates`) OR `the application has been served on that other person`)
       AND `s 276.01(4) the copy was given and filed at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows` `the day the application was served` `the day of the hearing` `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The accused shall serve the application on the prosecutor, on the complainant or witness"

-- The accused's duty as a rule, with its period: WITHIN the days from the day the application is made until 60 days before the hearing. Where the judge allows a shorter interval the text gives its length to the judge: no period is stated here.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.21(5)
-- src:5447 | Service of application
-- src:5448 | (5) The accused shall serve the application on the prosecutor, on the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and on any other person to whom, to the knowledge of the accused, the record or therapeutic record relates, at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in subsection 278.22(1) or within any shorter interval that the judge may allow in the interests of justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.21(5) (src:5447-5448)
GIVEN `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.21(5) the accused's duty to serve the application` MEANS
    IF `the judge allows a shorter interval in the interests of justice`
    THEN FULFILLED   -- the interval is the judge's to allow and the text states no length: no period is stated here (not a finding that the duty is met)
    ELSE PARTY `the accused`
         MUST `s 278.21(5) serve the application on the persons the subsection names`
         WITHIN (`s 270 helper: the days from the earlier date to the later date` `the day the application is made` `the day of the hearing` MINUS 60)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 278.21(5): the application was not served at least 60 days before the hearing"

