§ `Part VIII -- Order for production to the accused (s 278.25)`

-- (1) a record: the judge MAY order it produced to the accused if satisfied that it is likely relevant and that production is necessary in the interests of justice (a "may" function with an "if" gate: NOTHING when it fails).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.25(1)
-- src:5482 | Order — production of record to accused
-- src:5483 | 278.25 (1) If the judge is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify and its production is necessary in the interests of justice, the judge may order that the record, or the part, that is likely relevant be produced to the accused, subject to any conditions that may be imposed under subsection (4).
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(1) (src:5482-5483)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that its production is necessary in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.25(1) the judge may order the record to be produced to the accused` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify` AND `the judge is satisfied that its production is necessary in the interests of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge is satisfied that the record, or part of it, is likely relevant to an issue at trial or to the competence of a witness to testify and that its production is necessary in the interests of justice, the judge may order"

-- (2) a therapeutic record: the judge MAY order it produced to the accused if satisfied that it contains evidence likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt and not available from any other source.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.25(2)
-- src:5484 | Order — production of therapeutic record to accused
-- src:5485 | (2) If the judge is satisfied that the therapeutic record, or part of it, contains evidence that is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused’s guilt and that is not available from any other source, the judge may order that the therapeutic record, or the part, be produced to the accused, subject to any conditions that may be imposed under subsection (4).
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(2) (src:5484-5485)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the therapeutic record, or part of it, contains evidence that is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the evidence is not available from any other source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.25(2) the judge may order the therapeutic record to be produced to the accused` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that the therapeutic record, or part of it, contains evidence that is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt` AND `the judge is satisfied that the evidence is not available from any other source`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge is satisfied that the therapeutic record, or part of it, contains evidence that is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt and that is not available from any other source, the judge may order"

-- (3): the judge shall take the factors of s 278.23(2)(a) to (h) into account (the same enumeration).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.25(3)
-- src:5486 | Factors to be considered
-- src:5487 | (3) In determining whether to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused, the judge shall consider the salutary and deleterious effects of the determination on the accused’s right to make a full answer and defence and on the right to privacy, personal security and equality of the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and of any other person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates and, in particular, shall take the factors set out in paragraphs 278.23(2)(a) to (h) into account.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(3) (src:5486-5487)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 278.14(2) factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.25(3) the judge shall take the factor into account` MEANS
    `s 278.14(2) the judge shall take the factor into account` factor

-- src:5488 | Conditions
-- src:5489 | (4) If the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused, the judge may impose conditions on the production to protect the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests of the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and of any other person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates, including, for example, the following conditions:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(4) (src:5488-5489)
DECLARE `s 278.25(4) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.25(4)(a) that the record or therapeutic record be edited as directed by the judge`
    `s 278.25(4)(b) that a copy of the record or therapeutic record, rather than the original, be produced`
    `s 278.25(4)(c) that the accused and counsel for the accused not disclose the contents of the record or therapeutic record to any other person, except with the approval of the court`
    `s 278.25(4)(d) that the record or therapeutic record be viewed only at the offices of the court`
    `s 278.25(4)(e) that no copies of the record or therapeutic record be made or that restrictions be imposed on the number of copies of it that may be made`
    `s 278.25(4)(f) that information regarding any person named in the record or therapeutic record, such as their address, telephone number and place of employment, be severed from the record or therapeutic record`
    `s 278.25(4) another condition`

-- (4): the judge MAY impose conditions on the production "to protect the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests" ... "including, for example," the six listed.
-- A listed condition is JUST TRUE; another is JUST TRUE only if it protects those interests; NOTHING otherwise and outside an order for production to the accused.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.25(4); s 278.25(4)(a); s 278.25(4)(b); s 278.25(4)(c); s 278.25(4)(d); s 278.25(4)(e); s 278.25(4)(f)
-- src:5488 | Conditions
-- src:5489 | (4) If the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused, the judge may impose conditions on the production to protect the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests of the complainant or witness, as the case may be, and of any other person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates, including, for example, the following conditions:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(4) (src:5488-5489)
GIVEN condition IS A `s 278.25(4) condition`
      `the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition protects the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests of the complainant or witness and of any other person to whom the record relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.25(4) the judge may impose the condition on the production` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge orders the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused, the judge may impose conditions on the production"
        IF condition EQUALS `s 278.25(4) another condition` AND NOT `the condition protects the interests of justice and, to the greatest extent possible, the privacy, personal security and equality interests of the complainant or witness and of any other person to whom the record relates` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "including, for example, the following conditions"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "The record or therapeutic record, or the part of it, that is produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1) must not be used in any other proceedings."
-- The text names only an order under subsection (1) (a record), not subsection (2) (a therapeutic record): encoded as written (finding in NOTES.md). JUST TRUE: use in other proceedings is barred.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.25(5)
-- src:5496 | Restriction on use
-- src:5497 | (5) The record or therapeutic record, or the part of it, that is produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1) must not be used in any other proceedings.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(5) (src:5496-5497)
GIVEN `it was produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used in other proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.25(5) the use in other proceedings is barred` MEANS
    IF `it was produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1)` AND `it is used in other proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1) must not be used in any other proceedings"

-- The restriction as a rule: the accused SHANT use the produced record in any other proceedings; no time limit, so no WITHIN.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.25(5)
-- src:5496 | Restriction on use
-- src:5497 | (5) The record or therapeutic record, or the part of it, that is produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1) must not be used in any other proceedings.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(5) (src:5496-5497)
GIVEN `it was produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.25(5) the accused's prohibition on use in other proceedings` MEANS
    IF `it was produced to the accused under an order under subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY `the accused`
         SHANT `s 278.25(5) use the record in any other proceedings`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 278.25(5): the record produced to the accused was used in other proceedings"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no prohibition arises under this section on these facts (the decision function answers NOTHING there)

-- "If the judge refuses to order the production ..., the record ... must, unless a court orders otherwise, be kept in a sealed package by the court until the later of the end of the time for any appeal and the completion of any appeal in the proceedings
-- against the accused, at which time the record ... must be returned to the prosecutor or the person lawfully entitled to possession or control of it." The "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): JUST TRUE before the later day, JUST FALSE on and after it (when the return falls due).
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.25(6)
-- src:5498 | Retention by court
-- src:5499 | (6) If the judge refuses to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused, the record or therapeutic record, or the part, must, unless a court orders otherwise, be kept in a sealed package by the court until the later of the end of the time for any appeal and the completion of any appeal in the proceedings against the accused, at which time the record or therapeutic record, or the part, must be returned to the prosecutor or the person lawfully entitled to possession or control of it.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.25(6) (src:5498-5499)
GIVEN `the judge refuses to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the time for any appeal ends` IS A DATE
      `the day any appeal is completed` IS A DATE
      today IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.25(6) the record must still be kept in a sealed package by the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge refuses to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge refuses to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, to the accused"
        IF `a court orders otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a court orders otherwise"
        IF today BELOW (IF `the day the time for any appeal ends` ABOVE `the day any appeal is completed` THEN `the day the time for any appeal ends` ELSE `the day any appeal is completed`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the later of the end of the time for any appeal and the completion of any appeal in the proceedings against the accused"

§ `Part VIII -- Reasons for decision (s 278.26)`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.26(1)
-- src:5500 | Reasons for decision
-- src:5501 | 278.26 (1) The judge shall provide reasons for ordering or refusing to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, under subsection 278.23(1) or 278.25(1) or (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 278.26(1) (src:5500-5501)
GIVEN `the judge orders or refuses to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, under subsection 278.23(1) or 278.25(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.26(1) the judge shall provide reasons for ordering or refusing to order production` MEANS
    IF `the judge orders or refuses to order the production of the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, under subsection 278.23(1) or 278.25(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
