§ `Part VIII -- Publication prohibited (s 278.27)`

-- The exception of s 278.27(1.1) is word for word that of s 276.03(1.1): the same function serves.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.27(1.1); s 278.27(1.1)(a); s 278.27(1.1)(b); s 278.27(1.1)(c)
-- src:5509 | Exception
-- src:5510 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure of any information referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) to (c) is
-- src:5511 | (a) made in the course of the administration of justice when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known in the community;
-- src:5512 | (b) made by the complainant or any witness and about that complainant or witness and their particulars, in any forum and for any purpose, and they did not intentionally or recklessly reveal the identity of or reveal particulars likely to identify any other person whose identity is protected by this section; or
-- src:5513 | (c) made by the complainant or any witness when the purpose of the disclosure is not one of making the information known to the public, including when the disclosure is made to a legal professional, a health care professional or a person in a relationship of trust with the complainant or the witness.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.27(1.1) (src:5509-5513)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 276.03(1.1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.27(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    `s 276.03(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure` facts

-- src:5504 | Publication prohibited
-- src:5505 | 278.27 (1) No person shall publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following:
-- src:5506 | (a) the contents of an application made under subsection 278.21(1);
-- src:5507 | (b) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection 278.22(1) or 278.24(2);
-- src:5508 | (c) the determination of the judge under subsection 278.23(1) or 278.25(1) or (2) and the reasons provided under section 278.26, unless the judge, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right to privacy of the person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates, orders that the determination and the reasons may be published, broadcast or transmitted.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.27(1) (src:5504-5508)
DECLARE `s 278.27(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.27(1)(a) the contents of an application made under subsection 278.21(1)`
    `s 278.27(1)(b) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection 278.22(1) or 278.24(2)`
    `s 278.27(1)(c) the determination of the judge under subsection 278.23(1) or 278.25(1) or (2) and the reasons provided under section 278.26`
    `s 278.27(1) any other matter`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.27(1); s 278.27(1)(a); s 278.27(1)(b); s 278.27(1)(c)
-- src:5504 | Publication prohibited
-- src:5505 | 278.27 (1) No person shall publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following:
-- src:5506 | (a) the contents of an application made under subsection 278.21(1);
-- src:5507 | (b) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection 278.22(1) or 278.24(2);
-- src:5508 | (c) the determination of the judge under subsection 278.23(1) or 278.25(1) or (2) and the reasons provided under section 278.26, unless the judge, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right to privacy of the person to whom the record or therapeutic record relates, orders that the determination and the reasons may be published, broadcast or transmitted.
@ref Criminal Code s 278.27(1) (src:5504-5508)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 278.27(1) matter`
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right of privacy, that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is that evidence is admissible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is within subsection (1.1), by s 278.27(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.27(1) the publication, broadcast or transmission of the matter is prohibited` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 278.27(1) any other matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person shall not publish in any document, or broadcast or transmit in any way, any of the following"
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF `the disclosure is within subsection (1.1), by s 278.27(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the disclosure of any information referred to in paragraphs"
            IF `the disclosure is within subsection (1.1), by s 278.27(1.1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of the exception is itself not covered
            IF `the matter has an unless-clause that is met` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless"
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the matter has an unless-clause that is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER matter
            WHEN `s 278.27(1)(a) the contents of an application made under subsection 278.21(1)` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `s 278.27(1)(b) any evidence taken, information given or submissions made at a hearing under subsection 278.22(1) or 278.24(2)` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `s 278.27(1)(c) the determination of the judge under subsection 278.23(1) or 278.25(1) or (2) and the reasons provided under section 278.26` THEN `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has ordered, after taking into account the interests of justice and the right of privacy, that it may be published, broadcast or transmitted`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

