-- (1): "Except in accordance with this section, no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant that is in the possession or control of the accused -- and which the accused intends to adduce -- shall be admitted in evidence".
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.29(1)
-- src:5520 | Admissibility — possession by accused
-- src:5521 | 278.29 (1) Except in accordance with this section, no record or therapeutic record relating to a complainant that is in the possession or control of the accused — and which the accused intends to adduce — shall be admitted in evidence in any proceedings in respect of any of the following offences or in any proceedings in respect of two or more offences at least one of which is any of the following offences:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.29(1) (src:5520-5521)
