-- src:5529 | Factors to be considered
-- src:5530 | (3) In determining whether the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection (2), the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall take into account the following factors:
@ref Criminal Code s 278.29(3) (src:5529-5530)
DECLARE `s 278.29(3) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 278.29(3)(a) the interests of justice, including the right of the accused to make a full answer and defence`
    `s 278.29(3)(b) society's interest in encouraging the reporting of sexual assault offences`
    `s 278.29(3)(c) society's interest in encouraging the obtaining of treatment by complainants of sexual offences`
    `s 278.29(3)(d) whether there is a reasonable prospect that the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, will assist in arriving at a just determination in the case`
    `s 278.29(3)(e) the need to remove from the fact-finding process any discriminatory belief or bias`
    `s 278.29(3)(f) the risk that the evidence may unduly arouse sentiments of prejudice, sympathy or hostility in the jury`
    `s 278.29(3)(g) the potential prejudice to the complainant's personal dignity and right of privacy`
    `s 278.29(3)(h) the right of the complainant and of every individual to personal security and to the full protection and benefit of the law`
    `s 278.29(3)(i) any other factor that the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers relevant`

-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.29(3); s 278.29(3)(a); s 278.29(3)(b); s 278.29(3)(c); s 278.29(3)(d); s 278.29(3)(e); s 278.29(3)(f); s 278.29(3)(g); s 278.29(3)(h); s 278.29(3)(i)
