    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 278.29(3)(i) any other factor that the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers relevant` THEN
        IF `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers the factor relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other factor that the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers relevant"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): "inadmissible in whole or in part unless the judge ... determines, in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 278.3, 278.31 or 278.35, (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ...".
-- JUST TRUE: inadmissible (a condition of the "unless" is unmet); JUST FALSE: the "unless" is met.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.29(2); s 278.29(2)(a); s 278.29(2)(b); s 278.29(2)(c)
-- src:5524 | Requirements for admissibility
-- src:5525 | (2) The record or therapeutic record is inadmissible in whole or in part unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice determines, in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 278.3, 278.31 or 278.35,
@ref Criminal Code s 278.29(2) (src:5524-5525)
GIVEN `the thing is a therapeutic record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its admissibility is subject to section 276` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has made a determination in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 278.3, 278.31 or 278.35` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is that the evidence meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is that the record, or part of it, is relevant to an issue at trial and has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination is that the therapeutic record, or part of it, is evidence that is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt and there is no other evidence that is capable of raising a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.29(2) the record or therapeutic record is inadmissible` MEANS
    IF     `the judge, provincial court judge or justice has made a determination in accordance with the procedures set out in sections 278.3, 278.31 or 278.35`
       AND ((NOT `its admissibility is subject to section 276`) OR `the determination is that the evidence meets the conditions set out in subsection 276(2) while taking into account the factors set out in subsection (3)`)
       AND (IF `the thing is a therapeutic record`
            THEN `the determination is that the therapeutic record, or part of it, is evidence that is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt and there is no other evidence that is capable of raising a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt`
            ELSE `the determination is that the record, or part of it, is relevant to an issue at trial and has significant probative value that is not substantially outweighed by the danger of prejudice to the proper administration of justice`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is inadmissible in whole or in part unless the judge, provincial court judge or justice determines"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

