      `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers an application under subsection 278.3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 278.12 act`
`s 278.3(4) the presiding officer's duty to exclude the jury and the public` MEANS
    IF `s 278.3(4) the jury and the public shall be excluded when the application is considered` `the judge, provincial court judge or justice considers an application under subsection 278.3(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY presiding
         MUST `s 278.3(4) consider the application with the jury and the public excluded`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY presiding BECAUSE "s 278.3(4): the application was considered with the jury or the public present"
    ELSE FULFILLED   -- no duty arises on these facts: this is not a finding about any other case (the decision function answers NOTHING there)


