    `s 270 helper: every one of these holds` (LIST `the application meets the requirements of form and content, by s 278.3(2)`, JUST (`the copy was given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk at least 60 days previously or within a shorter interval that the judge allows`), JUST (`the record or therapeutic record, or the part of it, sought to be adduced is capable of being admissible`))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge, provincial court judge or justice is satisfied that the application was made in accordance with subsection (2), that a copy of the application was given to the prosecutor and filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days previously"; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of subsection (2) is itself not covered

