-- (4): the determination and the reasons: (a) if not all of the record is to be admitted, the part; (b) the factors of subsection 278.29(3) that affected the determination; (c) if all or any part of the record is to be admitted, the manner in which it is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial;
-- (d) if all or any part of the therapeutic record is to be admitted, how it is likely to raise a reasonable doubt and why there is no other evidence capable of raising one.
-- COVERS[encoded]: s 278.31(4); s 278.31(4)(a); s 278.31(4)(b); s 278.31(4)(c); s 278.31(4)(d)
-- src:5561 | Determination and reasons
-- src:5562 | (4) At the conclusion of the hearing, the judge, provincial court judge or justice shall determine whether the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) and shall provide reasons for that determination, and
@ref Criminal Code s 278.31(4) (src:5561-5562)
GIVEN `the judge has determined whether the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has provided reasons for that determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not all of the record or therapeutic record is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the part of it that is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3) that affected the determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or any part of the record is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state the manner in which it is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or any part of the therapeutic record is to be admitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons state how it is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt and why the judge is of the opinion that there is no other evidence that is capable of raising a reasonable doubt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 278.31(4) the determination and reasons meet the requirements` MEANS
    IF     `the judge has determined whether the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2)`
       AND `the judge has provided reasons for that determination`
       AND ((NOT `not all of the record or therapeutic record is to be admitted`) OR `the reasons state the part of it that is to be admitted`)
       AND `the reasons state the factors referred to in subsection 278.29(3) that affected the determination`
       AND ((NOT `all or any part of the record is to be admitted`) OR `the reasons state the manner in which it is expected to be relevant to an issue at trial`)
       AND ((NOT `all or any part of the therapeutic record is to be admitted`) OR `the reasons state how it is likely to raise a reasonable doubt as to the accused's guilt and why the judge is of the opinion that there is no other evidence that is capable of raising a reasonable doubt`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall determine whether the record or therapeutic record, or part of it, is admissible under subsection 278.29(2) and shall provide reasons for that determination"

